-- Chapter 1: Ancient Assam: Pragjyotisha and Kamarupa
Mlechchha dynasty: founded by Salasthambha (ruled 655 to 670 CE). Capital: Haruppeswara, near present-day Tezpur.
Pala dynasty: began with Brahma Pala (ruled 900 to 920 CE). Ratna Pala moved the capital to Durjaya.$t$ from public.content where slug = $t$ancient-assam-kamarupa$t$ on conflict do nothing;
ম্লেচ্ছ ৰাজবংশ: প্ৰতিষ্ঠাপক শালস্তম্ভ (৬৫৫ ৰ পৰা ৬৭০ খ্ৰীষ্টাব্দ)। ৰাজধানী: বৰ্তমানৰ তেজপুৰৰ ওচৰৰ হাৰুপ্পেশ্বৰ।
পাল ৰাজবংশ: ব্ৰহ্মপালৰ পৰা আৰম্ভ (৯০০ ৰ পৰা ৯২০ খ্ৰীষ্টাব্দ)। ৰত্নপালে ৰাজধানী দুৰ্জয়ালৈ স্থানান্তৰ কৰে।$t$ from public.content where slug = $t$ancient-assam-kamarupa$t$ on conflict do nothing;

-- Chapter 2: The Ahom kingdom (1228 to 1826)
Garhgaon (1540 to 1707)
Rangpur (1707 to 1794)
Jorhat (1794 to 1826)$t$ from public.content where slug = $t$ahom-kingdom$t$ on conflict do nothing;
Pratap Singha (1603 to 1641): reorganised the Paik system and created the offices of {{term:borphukan|Borphukan}} and Borbarua.
Rudra Singha (1696 to 1714): the kingdom reached its peak under him.
Pramatta Singha (1744 to 1751): built the Rang Ghar with masonry.$t$ from public.content where slug = $t$ahom-kingdom$t$ on conflict do nothing;
