In 1857, Maniram Dewan planned a rising to bring back Ahom rule. The plot was discovered, and he was hanged with Piyali Barua at Jorhat jail on 26 February 1858.
The Phulaguri Dhewa (1861): farmers at Phulaguri, near Nagaon, rose against new taxes, including a tax on betel leaf and areca nut. Lieutenant Singer, a British officer, was killed on 18 October 1861.$t$ from public.content where slug = $t$assam-under-british-rule$t$ on conflict do nothing;
